+
+### Cross-check of Judiciary’s three dispositions
+
+The Judiciary disposition's three-way status claims are internally consistent with its documented scope. Clerk unresolved is supported by the specific observation/reconciliation/terminal references it names; Executive remains inconclusive for missing successor/effects evidence; Innovation Centre remains inconclusive despite predecessor-effect evidence because exact successor progress is absent. These are findings about evidence sufficiency and handoff obligations, not proof the historic outages persist. I cannot independently vouch for all underlying source facts in those records from the disposition alone; the explicit citations make them checkable but are not substitutes for reinspection of the original observation/terminal artifacts.
+
+The historical case objects and index remain unreconciled in the observed snapshot. This is a **tracker completeness / evidence-disposition gap**, not an operational recovery test. The exact Judiciary-case recovery claim remains **inconclusive** pending independent case-linked observations; absence from the active index is a tracking defect, not evidence of recovery.
